### Set generation parameters in generateText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/providers/05-community-providers/24-llama-cpp.mdx

Passes standard AI SDK generation settings such as maxTokens, temperature, topP, topK, and stopSequences.

```ts
const { text } = await generateText({
  model,
  prompt: 'Hello!',
  maxTokens: 256,
  temperature: 0.7,
  topP: 0.9,
  topK: 40,
  stopSequences: ['\n'],
});
```

--------------------------------

### Configuring common settings in generateText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/03-ai-sdk-core/25-settings.mdx

Pass common options such as maxOutputTokens, temperature, maxRetries, and timeout into AI SDK calls. If a provider does not support a setting, check the warnings property on the result object.

```ts
const result = await generateText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  maxOutputTokens: 512,
  temperature: 0.3,
  maxRetries: 5,
  timeout: 10000,
  prompt: 'Invent a new holiday and describe its traditions.',
});
```

--------------------------------

### Pass vertex providerOptions with safetySettings to generateText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/providers/01-ai-sdk-providers/16-google-vertex.mdx

Pass model-specific configurations such as safetySettings using providerOptions.vertex in generateText. Use GoogleLanguageModelOptions from @ai-sdk/google to type-check the options object.

```ts
import { googleVertex } from '@ai-sdk/google-vertex';
import { type GoogleLanguageModelOptions } from '@ai-sdk/google';

const model = googleVertex('gemini-3.1-pro-preview');

await generateText({
  model,
  providerOptions: {
    vertex: {
      safetySettings: [
        {
          category: 'HARM_CATEGORY_UNSPECIFIED',
          threshold: 'BLOCK_LOW_AND_ABOVE',
        },
      ],
    } satisfies GoogleLanguageModelOptions,
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Attach onStart and onEnd callbacks to generateText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/03-ai-sdk-core/65-lifecycle-callbacks.mdx

Pass lifecycle callbacks directly into AI SDK calls like generateText to inspect execution metadata, model IDs, finish reasons, and token usage. Callbacks can be synchronous or asynchronous, and internal error handling ensures threw errors do not interrupt the main call.

```tsx
import { generateText } from 'ai';
__PROVIDER_IMPORT__;

const result = await generateText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  prompt: 'What is the weather in San Francisco?',

  onStart({ callId, modelId }) {
    console.log('Generation started', { callId, modelId });
  },

  onEnd({ callId, usage, finishReason }) {
    console.log('Generation finished', {
      callId,
      finishReason,
      totalTokens: usage.totalTokens,
    });
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Migrate output in AI SDK 7

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/08-migration-guides/23-migration-guide-7-0.mdx

Shows structured outputs using the standard output option and result.output in AI SDK 7.

```tsx
const result = await generateText({
  model: yourModel,
  output: Output.object({
    schema: recipeSchema,
  }),
  prompt: 'Generate a recipe.',
});

console.log(result.output);
```

